                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "very enjoyable, enticing and exiting... if you have patience. this game is extremely fun to the point where it almost has infinite replayability as it has a mission editor where i have spent numerous hours on making missions just for the fun of it. the campaign missions, single missions and multiplayer (on LAN) are also really fun too. if you play this yourself you gotta agree the tension in the air (or water, whichever way you look at it) gives you a shiver down your spine.\n\nmy only complaint is the game is a bit boring as you enter a sub, go around for like 5-25 minutes looking for another vessel (even on 2x speed), identify it as a neutral cargo ship and then just move back onto your original course. this can take up a very long time of gameplay, but still, i believe the combat pays off.\n\ni'd give the AI a solid 7/10, as the aircraft, surface and submarine ai can all get the job done in taking out an enemy, but still i think Silent Hunter III did it the best. \n\nin conclusion i think the game is ace, but definitely requires patience, but trust me.. once you get into a confrontation you'll have a totally different view of the game.",
